\pard\sb0\sa240\qc\b\f0\fs32\cf1 COLON NOT FOLLOWED BY QUOTATION\par
\pard\sb0\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 PURPOSE\par
\pard\sb0\sa120\b0\f0\fs20\cf0 Finds places where a colon is followed by text that does not begin with a quotation mark. This catches dialogue or quoted speech that may be missing its opening quotation mark.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 HOW TO USE\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\b0\f0\fs20 1.\tab Copy the .cms and .py files to your My Paratext 9 Projects\\cms folder.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 2.\tab In Paratext, run the check from Project menu > Tools > Custom Tools > Phil_new.\par
\pard\li720\fi-360\sb0\sa80\f0\fs20 3.\tab Review the results; each flagged item shows the colon and the text that follows it without a quotation mark.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80\keepn\b\f0\fs22\cf2 OPTIONS\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 QuotationMarks\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i <<  "  --  '}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 The characters that your translation uses to open a quotation. If the word after a colon starts with one of these characters it is not flagged. Update this to match your project's quotation style.\par
\pard\li360\sb160\sa0\keepn\b\f1\fs20\cf3 CapitalizedOnly\par
\pard\li720\sb60\sa0\b0\f0\fs20{\b Default:}  {\i Yes}\par
\pard\li720\sb40\sa80\f0\fs20 When Yes, only flags cases where the first word after the colon begins with a capital letter. Set to No to flag all words regardless of case.\par
}
